{
  "id": "lorenzoscaturchio/spotify-tracks-audio-features-50k",
  "title": "Spotify Tracks: Audio Features (50K Songs)",
  "subtitle": "50K tracks with audio features, popularity, and genre labels",
  "description": "50,000 synthetic Spotify-style tracks spanning 2000\u20132024 across 20 genres. Each row includes track metadata plus the core Spotify-style audio features used for recommendation, clustering, and predictive modeling: danceability, energy, loudness, speechiness, acousticness, instrumentalness, liveness, valence, tempo, key, mode, and time signature.\n\nBuilt for popularity prediction, genre classification, playlist mood clustering, trend analysis, and recommender-system prototyping. The dataset is intentionally lightweight enough for notebook workflows while still large enough to support non-trivial tabular ML experiments.\n\nNotable properties: genre-aware feature correlations, Zipf-like popularity distribution, realistic tempo ranges, and synthetic generation designed for educational benchmarking rather than exact catalog reconstruction.",
